---
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Setting a winter table — AASRA Journal" description="Candlelight, stoneware, and the case for long dinners.">
  <div class="page-title-block">
    <div class="kicker">Journal · At home</div>
    <h1>Setting a winter table</h1>
    <p class="page-sub">Composing a table for the season.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px;">
      <img src="/images/campaign/banner-table.webp" alt="A candlelit winter tablescape" loading="eager" width="1600" height="1000" style="width:100%; aspect-ratio:16/10; object-fit:cover; display:block; margin-bottom:2.5rem;" />

      <div class="prose">
        <p>Winter tables are set differently — lower light, heavier ceramic, more time. The season asks for dinners that run long, and a table that makes staying easy.</p>
        <p>Start with texture, not colour. Speckled stoneware against a natural linen cloth does more than any centerpiece; the plates carry the theme. Mix depths instead of patterns — the serving bowl's wide rim beside the dinner plate's tight speckle reads as intentional.</p>
        <p>Candlelight should sit low, in glass holders, at three heights and uneven intervals. Even spacing reads as a restaurant; scatter reads as a home. Teak boards and trays belong in the middle of the table, not the kitchen — bread, olives, and things to share give hands somewhere to rest between conversations.</p>
        <p>And set the table early in the day. A table that is ready at noon changes how the whole house feels by evening — it makes the dinner itself inevitable.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="service-links" style="justify-content:flex-start; margin-top:2.5rem;">
        <a href="/shop?category=tableware">Shop the tableware</a>
        <a href="/journal">Back to the Journal</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose p { color: var(--muted); line-height: 2; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .prose p:first-of-type { color: var(--text); font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.7; }
</style>
